  <Properties>
    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[As front-end applications grow in complexity, establishing a clear, scalable architecture is essential. But with the ever-evolving landscape of front-end development, how do you design systems that are both flexible and maintainable over time? This session will explore common patterns in front-end architecture, focusing on strategies for building apps that are easy to scale, update, and debug.

We’ll dive into the foundational principles of front-end architecture, including modularity, componentization, and separation of concerns. Then, we will look at how we can apply those principles to patterns such as atomic design and event-driven architecture.]]></Value>
    </description>
